{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T21:57:55.152Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"350da2812dfbdc6e7a54c37f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-07T21:57:55.152Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Exact stored-value checks exposed SDK normalization: empty assignee strings and empty dependency arrays become absent in canonical reads/writes. The record now saves both canonical prior state and original representation/format. Compensation restores canonical state through mutateItem, then uses SDK item lock, atomic file write, and append-only history primitives to preserve original physical fields at the same verified canonical hash. Its final completion receipt follows that write. Seven focused built-package, empty-representation, phase-crash, and writer-gap scenarios passed; a real SIGKILL between update and close also passed. No SDK issue was filed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T21:57:55.152Z"}],"before_hash":"4488a9bc19fe50a54847e83a1755b5b8b2cea2d9ec095ddd532114f25ceb03d1","after_hash":"66d169d5c2651d67f3b7c51d008c41eac1aaedb5bdc31c294e09821623a96ebd","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0907b236f7fa7b6ac88e617d3ca4364e1b6ef0233d62718ab71d2377ef881b75"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T22:04:45.050Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"350da2812dfbdc6e7a54c37f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-07T22:04:45.050Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Behavioral revert proof: an isolated copy retained the same index, tests and SDK, built successfully, and replaced only compensateUpdate's body with its previous no-op behavior. All three selected tests failed on behavioral assertions (two built-package exact-state cases retained Changed/priority 3/type Feature/lifecycle changes; the independent-writer case lacked the required refusal). The current implementation passed the focused exact-state and writer checks. Existing subprocess fixtures were given a local CommonJS package boundary so an ancestor ESM setting cannot prevent their failure injections from loading."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T22:04:45.050Z"}],"before_hash":"66d169d5c2651d67f3b7c51d008c41eac1aaedb5bdc31c294e09821623a96ebd","after_hash":"c1bd8cf8ff43203716c7dc32ecbebcee641afcc0f8a786dd5d2693e7542f81a3","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c95b10bbdf415f30cb6f21523e5e31bb1c0c3cdb5118f156299ad17529354baa"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T22:25:21.524Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"350da2812dfbdc6e7a54c37f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-07T22:25:21.524Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"The PM-linked suite passed 32/32 real-tracker scenarios. A further red regression showed restart could lose the update target after another writer replaced all CSV tags. Versioned step identities now bind operation, target id, and row; replay recovers those immutable bindings from the SDK journal. The removed-tags scenario, legacy refusal, keyed resume, rollback retry, and closed-row resume passed 5/5 focused checks. npm/Bun/current and npm/minimum packed acceptance also passed. SDK gaps handled locally: canonical normalization of empty fields and bulk restore without a concurrent-writer guard."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T22:25:21.524Z"}],"before_hash":"c1bd8cf8ff43203716c7dc32ecbebcee641afcc0f8a786dd5d2693e7542f81a3","after_hash":"98a25e5a38e48526ecbd13a5c9ae4bb6672a75bc5b6c59621c4b301464fd93bd","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"43b1832741bcfe9f1f64b9e49e7f791a975d8855b7a6593809dd5d934b8167b5"}
